  "answer": "DIAGNOSIS (verified from the live app and observability before any code change)\nFailing request: POST /api/checkout?currencyCode=USD returned a plain-text HTTP 500 \"Internal Server Error\". Correlated evidence:\n- Browser: console SyntaxError from JSON.parse on the non-JSON 500 body (shared helper parsed any body, never checked response.ok).\n- Jaeger via Grafana proxy (/grafana/api/datasources/proxy/uid/webstore-traces): frontend span \"executing api route /api/checkout\" http.status_code=500, otel.status_code=ERROR, exception \"13 INTERNAL: ... could not charge the card ...\"; checkout span PlaceOrder error \"failed to charge card: could not charge the card: ... Payment request failed. Invalid token\"; payment span Charge error \"Payment request failed. Invalid token. demo.user_context.loyalty_level=gold\".\n- Payment service log (OpenSearch): \"Payment request failed: Invalid token\" at charge.js:47:15. Flagd UI (/feature) showed paymentFailure=on (paymentUnreachable/cartFailure off); product-catalog failure on OLJCESPC7Z and ad-service UNAVAILABLE were active concurrently (traces 378b9d26…, 30ff206b…). So the failing chain is frontend → checkout (PlaceOrder) → payment (Charge) under the paymentFailure flag.\n\nCHANGES (frontend only; no Docker/Compose/env/flag/unrelated service files touched)\n- src/frontend/pages/api/checkout.ts: POST handler wrapped in try/catch. Payment-charge failures (checkout's own marker \"could not charge the card\") → HTTP 422 with {error: \"Payment failed: the payment method was declined.\", code: \"PAYMENT_FAILED\"} (client-safe, no upstream details). All other failures → HTTP 500 with generic {error: \"Internal server error\"} (no code, no leaks). Both paths recordException + setStatus(ERROR) so failures stay visible in telemetry.\n- src/frontend/utils/Request.ts: helper now rejects non-success responses, preserves a JSON server \"error\" message, and safely handles non-JSON error bodies (no more JSON.parse SyntaxError).\n- New focused spec src/frontend/cypress/e2e/CheckoutErrorContract.cy.ts.\n- BENCHMARK_REPORT.md documents services, trace IDs, original failure, changes, outcomes and limitations.\n\nVERIFICATION (actual outcomes)\n- Redeploy via the benchmark tool succeeded (build + healthy container).\n- Live browser: add-to-cart → Place Order now yields POST /api/checkout => 422 with the client-safe message; console shows \"Error: Payment failed: the payment method was declined.\" and no JSON.parse crash.\n- Live Jaeger trace c682f13d53c6eae89a08f06575939126 after the fix: payment Charge error, checkout PlaceOrder error, frontend POST /api/checkout spans http.status_code=422 with recorded exception, Envoy 422 — error telemetry preserved.\n- New Cypress spec: 3/3 passing (payment 422/PAYMENT_FAILED; malformed-order 500 with exact generic body and no PAYMENT_FAILED/leaks; non-JSON 502 body handled without SyntaxError).\n- Existing specs Home.cy.ts/ProductDetail.cy.ts: 4/6 pass; the two failures (session-recovery race, missing-image assertion) are pre-existing and unrelated to the modified code paths. The old checkout happy-path test cannot pass while the live paymentFailure fault is active, by design.\n\nLIMITATIONS: decline detection uses checkout's own wrapper string (a gRPC-code-based classifier would need changes to the protected checkout service); paymentUnreachable would also map to 422 under this rule; collector's OpenSearch exporter drops some payment error logs due to a malformed attributes.err field (out of scope).",
